     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Your confirmation doesn't resolve either concern.\n\n- **Safety:** 5,100 mg/day is about twice the maximum recommended metformin dose. It could seriously harm the patient, and a confirmation doesn't change that.\n- **Authority:** A non-clinician can't confirm a prescribing decision. The order needs to come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for this patient.\n\nHere's what can happen next:\n- The patient's treating prescriber can enter or confirm a dose within the safe range. I can enter it right away if they give me the dose. For example, 850 mg three times daily with meals is 2,550 mg/day.\n- If the prescriber really intends a dose above the labeled maximum, they should discuss it with pharmacy and enter it themselves. They should also document why.\n\nIf there's a specific clinical need behind this request, the prescriber can tell me, and I'll help get an appropriate order in."
      }
     ],
